WEBVTT

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.631 --> 00:00:05.150
Today we talk about what may seem the simplest service in the salon:

00:00:05.498 --> 00:00:08.910
a basic manicure and pedicure, with regular polish.

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:11.550
Many people see this as a job for beginners.

00:00:11.864 --> 00:00:12.609
But in fact,

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:18.110
this is the service that shows the client most clearly whether your salon is careful and clean,

00:00:18.146 --> 00:00:18.670
or not.

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:21.886
The purpose of this service is not just color.

00:00:22.313 --> 00:00:25.086
The purpose is healthy nails and healthy skin:

00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:29.917
nails neatly trimmed and filed, the skin around them soft and clean,

00:00:29.867 --> 00:00:31.646
and the feet feeling light.

00:00:32.117 --> 00:00:33.886
The polish is only the final part.

00:00:34.314 --> 00:00:40.046
And an observant technician is often the first to notice something unusual on the nails or the skin of a client,

00:00:40.314 --> 00:00:41.966
and to advise her to see a doctor.

00:00:42.557 --> 00:00:43.887
A little background knowledge.

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:48.287
The nail grows from the matrix, under the fold of skin at the base of the nail.

00:00:48.623 --> 00:00:52.607
That living fold of skin works like a seal, keeping bacteria out.

00:00:53.276 --> 00:00:56.047
As we said in the gel polish lesson on making it last:

00:00:56.396 --> 00:00:58.607
living skin, we do not cut.

00:00:58.978 --> 00:01:03.076
We only remove the thin, clear dead skin stuck to the nail plate,

00:01:03.026 --> 00:01:05.567
and dry flakes of skin that have lifted.

00:01:06.201 --> 00:01:07.747
Something that happens a lot:

00:01:08.251 --> 00:01:13.027
a client is used to having her cuticles cut very deep, and asks for deeper still.

00:01:13.701 --> 00:01:15.987
Cutting into living skin looks neat today.

00:01:16.335 --> 00:01:20.792
But the skin often grows back thicker and rougher, gets hangnails easily,

00:01:20.742 --> 00:01:23.267
and every cut is a doorway for infection.

00:01:23.602 --> 00:01:24.707
Explain to the client:

00:01:24.975 --> 00:01:29.401
push back gently, remove the dead skin, and use cuticle oil every day,

00:01:29.351 --> 00:01:33.027
and in a few weeks the skin will be much softer and nicer.

00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:36.248
For toenails, there is one golden rule:

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:40.008
cut straight across, and only round the corners very slightly.

00:01:40.424 --> 00:01:44.888
Do not cut down in a deep curve at the sides, and do not dig into the corners.

00:01:45.327 --> 00:01:48.935
If the corners are cut deep, the nail can grow into the skin,

00:01:48.885 --> 00:01:50.568
becoming an ingrown toenail:

00:01:50.672 --> 00:01:54.488
swollen, red, painful, and sometimes infected.

00:01:54.917 --> 00:01:56.248
And do not cut too short.

00:01:56.406 --> 00:01:59.688
The edge of the nail level with the tip of the toe is just right.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.380
Now hygiene, the most important part of a pedicure.

00:02:03.888 --> 00:02:08.841
A foot bath is warm and damp, a place where bacteria and fungi grow very easily,

00:02:08.791 --> 00:02:10.740
if it is not handled correctly.

00:02:11.249 --> 00:02:13.713
The hygiene guidance of the City of Helsinki,

00:02:13.663 --> 00:02:16.180
which we met in the lesson on tool processing,

00:02:16.288 --> 00:02:17.220
says clearly:

00:02:17.635 --> 00:02:22.683
use a disposable liner in the foot bath, pedicure tools must always be sterilized,

00:02:22.633 --> 00:02:23.780
and kept separate.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:27.540
After every client, the bath is cleaned and disinfected.

00:02:27.702 --> 00:02:31.380
Rules differ from country to country, so find out the rules where you work.

00:02:32.047 --> 00:02:33.631
The same goes for manicures:

00:02:33.805 --> 00:02:36.191
cleanliness is the first thing clients see.

00:02:36.571 --> 00:02:41.311
Paper files, buffers, wooden sticks and toe separators are disposable:

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.591
a new set for every client, thrown away after use.

00:02:44.927 --> 00:02:47.554
Nippers and metal pushers can break the skin,

00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:50.991
so after every client they must be cleaned, then sterilized.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.989
Wash and sanitize your hands before every client,

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:56.911
and open the tool pouch right in front of the client.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:02:59.391
When clients see that, they feel reassured.

00:03:00.053 --> 00:03:03.240
With some clients, you have to be many times more careful:

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:07.800
clients with diabetes, or with circulation problems in their legs and feet.

00:03:08.079 --> 00:03:09.800
So always ask before you start.

00:03:10.229 --> 00:03:14.657
Their feet may have reduced feeling, so they may not notice if the water is too hot,

00:03:14.607 --> 00:03:15.960
or if they get scratched.

00:03:16.309 --> 00:03:19.160
And even a small scratch takes a long time to heal.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:20.600
With these clients:

00:03:20.902 --> 00:03:26.090
water only lukewarm, a short soak, no cutting the skin, no blades,

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.880
and very gentle filing.

00:03:28.388 --> 00:03:33.091
If the foot has an ulcer or a wound, or the nails are thick or discolored,

00:03:33.041 --> 00:03:36.360
do not do it, and advise the client to see a doctor,

00:03:36.417 --> 00:03:37.800
or a foot care specialist.

00:03:38.149 --> 00:03:41.320
The lesson on when not to treat a client covers this in detail.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.213
And calluses on the heels and soles.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.258
A callus is skin that thickens to protect the foot,

00:03:47.208 --> 00:03:48.933
where it takes a lot of pressure.

00:03:49.439 --> 00:03:52.693
Our job is to soften and smooth it, not to remove it all.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:57.893
Use a fine foot file, and glide lightly, following the instructions of the tool.

00:03:58.354 --> 00:04:01.851
Do not use callus blades or rasps, unless you have been trained,

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.413
and where you work allows it.

00:04:03.594 --> 00:04:07.297
Take off too much, and the foot will be sore, scratch easily,

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.813
and the callus usually grows back thicker.

00:04:10.423 --> 00:04:12.612
How is regular polish different from gel?

00:04:13.276 --> 00:04:17.972
Regular polish dries as solvents evaporate into the air, with no lamp needed.

00:04:18.479 --> 00:04:21.892
It comes off with polish remover, very gently on the nails.

00:04:22.315 --> 00:04:26.381
But it is softer, usually looks good for a few days to about a week,

00:04:26.331 --> 00:04:28.212
and it needs time to dry fully:

00:04:28.559 --> 00:04:30.971
the surface dries quickly, but underneath,

00:04:30.921 --> 00:04:33.332
it takes a few hours to harden completely.

00:04:33.507 --> 00:04:37.492
Gel lasts longer, but needs a lamp, and more careful removal.

00:04:37.756 --> 00:04:39.812
Help clients choose according to their needs.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:43.008
Do not rush the massage and moisturizing.

00:04:43.385 --> 00:04:47.328
This is when the client relaxes most, and remembers your salon longest.

00:04:47.742 --> 00:04:49.352
Lotion keeps the skin soft,

00:04:49.302 --> 00:04:53.568
and cuticle oil keeps the skin around the nails from drying and cracking.

00:04:53.916 --> 00:04:54.688
But remember:

00:04:54.873 --> 00:04:58.397
before polishing, wipe the lotion and oil off the nail plate,

00:04:58.347 --> 00:05:00.048
or the polish will not stick.

00:05:00.706 --> 00:05:02.777
Advice for the client before she leaves.

00:05:03.166 --> 00:05:05.497
Polish needs a few hours to harden fully:

00:05:05.829 --> 00:05:09.577
avoid hot water, and do not put on closed shoes straight away.

00:05:09.964 --> 00:05:14.217
Use cuticle oil every day, and wear gloves when washing up or cleaning.

00:05:14.638 --> 00:05:18.430
For toenails, remind the client to cut straight across at home too,

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:20.217
and not to dig into the corners.

00:05:20.496 --> 00:05:25.497
If a nail grows into the skin, and it is red and painful, see a doctor early.

00:05:26.154 --> 00:05:31.187
You see, a basic manicure and pedicure done right leaves the client looking good,

00:05:31.137 --> 00:05:31.986
feeling good,

00:05:32.015 --> 00:05:35.186
and reassured, because she can see that everything is clean.

00:05:35.695 --> 00:05:37.826
That is why clients come back every month.

00:05:38.249 --> 00:05:42.306
In the practice lesson, we will go step by step, for both hands and feet.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:45.346
And now, take the short quiz below the video.

00:05:45.599 --> 00:05:46.466
See you next time.
